<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Movement disorders neurology consultation to confirm the diagnosis against the MDS consensus classification, choose treatment, and advise on head and voice tremor. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018) [S]</item><item>Monitor at every visit: TETRAS performance and daily-living subscales, spiral drawing and handwriting, heart rate and standing blood pressure on propranolol, side effects, falls, and drugs that worsen tremor; yearly: examination for signs beyond tremor, mood, cognition, and an AGS Beers Criteria medication review. Focused ultrasound thalamotomy or deep brain stimulation is considered only if disabling limb tremor persists after adequate trials of propranolol and primidone. Guideline: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018); A Randomized Trial of Focused Ultrasound Thalamotomy for Essential Tremor (2016); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, general items for older adults (no essential tremor monograph) (2026) [S]</item><item>Advance care planning: name a health care agent and record goals of care at the annual wellness visit. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, general items for older adults (no essential tremor monograph) (2026) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to neurology (movement disorders), Tomasz Wierzbicki, MD, ordered 1980-01-13 [S]</item></list></text>

